   582	## 8. Patch Extraction & Phase 2 Verification (`verify_task`)
   583	
   584	### 8.1. How Patches Are Extracted (`submit_patch` & Automatic Fallback)
   585	Both explicit `submit_patch()` calls and the harness fallback run the exact same git commands inside `/workspace` in Container A:
   586	```bash
   587	cd /workspace && git add -N .
   588	cd /workspace && (git diff --binary _swegemma_baseline 2>/dev/null || git diff --binary HEAD)
   589	```
   590	1. **Why `git add -N .` Matters**: `--intent-to-add` registers any newly created untracked files in the git index with empty content so that **`git diff` includes both modifications to existing tracked files AND newly created files**, while still ignoring everything listed in `/workspace/.git/info/exclude` (`__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `.pytest_cache/`, `*.egg-info/`, `build/`, `dist/`, `.coverage`).
   591	2. **Protected Test & Config File Stripping (`strip_protected_files_from_patch`)**: Both `submit_patch()` and the unsubmitted-diff fallback strip any diff hunks touching protected test files (`test_*.py`, `*_test.py`, or `.py` files under `tests/`, `test/`, `testing/`) or runner configuration files (`conftest.py`, `pytest.ini`, `pyproject.toml`, `tox.ini`, `setup.cfg`, `.pytest.ini`, `sitecustomize.py`, `usercustomize.py`, `_swegemma_stubs.py`, `*.pth`) so temporary reproduction tests or runner config edits never pollute `agent_patch`.
   592	3. **Automatic Unsubmitted Patch Recovery (`agent_runner.py`, lines 760–805)**:
   593	   If an agent finishes, hits `max_nudges`, exhausts `tool_calls` or `turns`, or times out **without ever calling `submit_patch()`**, the harness automatically runs `git add -N .`, `git diff --binary _swegemma_baseline`, and `strip_protected_files_from_patch` before tearing down Container A.
   594	   - If the working tree contains non-empty modifications to non-protected files (`agent_patch != ""`), `Evaluator.evaluate_task` (`evaluate.py`) and `scripts/inference.py` still record `agent_patch` in `submission.parquet` (`[id, prediction]`) so it is evaluated in Phase 2 verification!
